Title: How do I register a generic base interface without name collisions?
Description: ## Summary

I want to do the following:

- Register an ``InterfaceGraphType<T> where T: IBaseEntity`` where ``IBaseEntity`` contains some very generic fields (Id, Created and Updated)
- Create an abstract generic base object to inherit from so that my object types does not have to implement the same fields over and over again
- Inherit this base object class from different types 
- I want the interface be the same for all objects implementing it. That is, i want them all to implement ``BaseEntityInterface`` and not ``BaseEntityInterface<TypeName>``.
    - I want to be able to click on the ``BaseEntityInterface`` in a documentation explorer and list all the types implementing this interface. That will not happen if a generic typename is generated for each implementation. Then there will be only one per interface.
  
Right now, if I use this approach I get a name collision telling me that the name is already registered (if I don´t generate unique names). So I guess I'm going about this in the wrong way...any hints? 

And I do, of course want to use the benefits of having generics so things get typechecked by the compiler.

I think the actions in #510, and #1284 prevents my use case (which I think is legit)?

## Relevant information

```csharp
 public class BaseEntityInterface<T> : InterfaceGraphType<T> where T: IBaseEntity
    {
        public BaseEntityInterface()
        {
            this.Description = "An entity with a id and created/updated timestamps";

            this.Field(x => x.Id)
                .Description("The unique identifier of the entitity.");
            this.Field(x => x.Created)
                .Description("Timestamp when the entity was first created.");
            this.Field(x => x.Updated)
                .Description("Timestamp when the entity was last updated.");
        }
    }

 public abstract class BaseEntityObject<T> : ObjectGraphType<T> where T: IBaseEntity
    {
        public BaseEntityObject()
        {
            this.Description = "An entity with a id and created/updated timestamps";


            this.Field(x => x.Id)
                .Description("The unique identifier of the entity.");
            this.Field(x => x.Created)
                .Description("Timestamp when the entity was first created.");
            this.Field(x => x.Updated)
                .Description("Timestamp when the entity was last updated.");

            this.Interface<BaseEntityInterface<T>>();
            this.IsTypeOf = obj => obj is IBaseEntity;
        }
    }

// Sample implementation type
public class InvoiceArticleObject: BaseEntityObject<InvoiceArticle>
    {
        public InvoiceArticleObject()
        {
            this.Description = "Invoice article.";

           // ...

            this.Interface<BaseEntityInterface<InvoiceArticle>>();
            this.IsTypeOf = obj => obj is InvoiceArticle;
        }
    }
   
```

